  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Participatory budget monitoring at district and national levels</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Timor Leste (TL) is Asia&#x2019;s youngest independent nation and citizens are limited in their opportunities and capacities to influence Government at both district and national levels. Civil society is at a crucial stage in its development where it can support citizens to engage with different levels of Government and the issues affecting their local communities, and furthermore to create opportunities and structures in which this empowerment can flourish. 

The Government of Timor Leste has at its disposal a wealth of oil and gas revenues. This project will support Luta Hamutuk to train citizens about national budgeting processes and how to monitor government expenditure on infrastructure projects at the local level. By bringing together citizens, Luta Hamutuk staff and local government representatives through district committees, local citizens will be able influence how the oil and gas revenues are spent, for the benefit of Timorese society.</narrative>
  </description>
